<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nghệ-Tĩnh Soviets</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1930–1931</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Nghe-Tinh Soviets, Nghe-Tinh uprising</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nghệ-Tĩnh Soviets were a peasant uprising in the provinces of Nghệ An and Hà Tĩnh in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in 1930–1931, organised with the help of the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochinese-communist-party">Indochinese Communist Party</a> during the Depression. Villagers set up local councils, seized land and stopped paying taxes. French forces crushed the movement with aerial bombing, executions and mass arrests, but it became a founding episode of Vietnamese communism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nghe-tinh-soviets.jpg" alt="Nghệ-Tĩnh Soviets" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arvn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Nghe_Tinh_Soviet_Movement.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
